OBJECTIVES:

1. To develop a menu-driven Contact Management System for maintaining contact records efficiently.
2. To store contact details such as contact ID, name and phone number in a doubly linked list.
3. To perform essential operations such as adding new contacts, searching for contact records, calling contacts, and displaying records.
4. To display contact information in both forward and backward directions using the doubly linked list.
5. To use a binary search tree to search contacts quickly by name and to display all contacts in alphabetical order using inorder traversal.
6. To use a graph (adjacency matrix array) to connect related contacts and to explore the contact network using BFS and DFS traversal.
7. To use a queue to maintain the call log in FIFO order and support removing the oldest call.
8. To apply dynamic memory allocation and linked-list operations for flexible record management, improving accuracy, accessibility and organization of contact information while reducing manual record-handling effort.
